{% psec 1, "The Strategy", "What is the Turtle Soup strategy, and why might it work?" %}
<p class="section-sub">Turtle Soup is an ICT (Inner Circle Trader) concept that <em>fades</em> the classic Turtle Trader breakout. Where traditional Turtle Traders buy new highs and sell new lows, Turtle Soup does the opposite — it anticipates false breakouts.</p>

<div class="card-grid">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-title">The setup</div>
    <div class="card-body">Price sweeps a recent N-day high or low, triggering breakout traders. It then reverses back inside the range — the "soup" — trapping those traders on the wrong side.</div>
    <span class="card-tag tag-blue">Liquidity sweep</span>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-title">Long signal</div>
    <div class="card-body">Price breaks below the N-day low (sweeps buy-side liquidity), then closes back above it within the same candle. Enter long at the next open.</div>
    <span class="card-tag tag-green">Bullish reversal</span>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-title">Short signal</div>
    <div class="card-body">Price breaks above the N-day high (sweeps sell-side liquidity), then closes back below it. Enter short at the next open.</div>
    <span class="card-tag tag-red">Bearish reversal</span>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-title">Stop & target</div>
    <div class="card-body">Stop loss placed at ATR × multiplier from entry. Take profit at R:R × stop distance. Both parameters are optimised in the grid search.</div>
    <span class="card-tag tag-amber">ATR-based sizing</span>
  </div>
</div>
{% endpsec %}

{% psec 2, "How the Model Works", "How was the backtest built and tuned?", "How It Works" %}
<div class="alert alert-blue">
  <div class="alert-title">Methodology</div>
  This is not just a simple backtest — it includes a full parameter optimisation pipeline with overfitting protection. Three years of data are split into in-sample (years \(1\text{–}2\)) and out-of-sample (year \(3\)). Parameters are optimised only on in-sample data and then validated on the unseen out-of-sample period.
</div>

